@namespace DYS.Molargo.Shared.Components

@*
    One field's validation message.

    Cross-cutting rather than a patient-form component: the booking form validates the
    same way, and a second copy of a null check is a second place for it to drift.

    Its own component because the pattern repeats on every validated field and the null
    check has to go with it — an empty coloured div under every clean input is invisible
    but still takes vertical space, which made the form's rows drift out of alignment
    column to column.

    Red, matching the failure notice at the top of the form rather than the accent it used
    to share with the save confirmation: a field message and the banner summarising it are
    the same event, and they should not have been two different colours.

    role="alert" so the message is announced when it appears rather than only being
    findable by someone who goes looking for it.
*@

@if (Message is { Length: > 0 })
{
    <div class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-accent2-700" role="alert">@Message</div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Null or empty when the field is fine, in which case nothing renders.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Message { get; set; }
}
